<article class="env-definition" id="0BGW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BGW">Definition <span data-tag="0BGW">68.11.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a decent algebraic space over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$. The <em>henselian local ring of $X$ at $x$</em>, is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_{X, x}^ h = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \Gamma (U, \mathcal{O}_ U)  \]
</div>
  <p> where the colimit is over the elementary étale neighbourhoods $(U, u) \to (X, x)$. </p>
</article>